    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d390">

                <pb facs="0385" n="269" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg269"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 123.G35/47a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the American Chargé d’Affaires</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-08-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 28, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Accept the Department’s congratulations for the very good work done by the
                    Legation.</p>
                <p>In regard to your August 27, the Department has communicated with the Cuban
                    Legation expressing its regret at the vicious and uncalled-for assault upon you
                    August 27 and has requested that the Cuban Government take prompt and vigorous
                    measures adequately to punish the offender. You will so inform the Cuban
                    Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
